5. World Chat Communication Network

Associated specification: WS-WC-001-IMP-01.

World Chat provides the communication and coordination layer.

5.1 Core modules

Module| Function
Personal Channel| Individual communication space
Call Cards| Contact and communication identifiers
Autolink| Controlled connection discovery
Signal| Standard notification
Sound| Higher-priority notification
Siren| Emergency notification
Mesh Transport| Local peer-to-peer communication
Store-and-Forward| Bounded offline message delivery
Channel Registry| Channel metadata and membership
Identity Service| Pseudonymous participant management

5.2 Communication architecture

The proposed architecture supports three operating conditions:

Connected mode: Internet-based communication and synchronization.

Local mesh mode: Direct communication between compatible nearby devices using supported transport technologies.

Intermittent mode: Local message preservation and later synchronization.

A browser application cannot assume access to unrestricted device-to-device radio capabilities. Android and web implementations will require separate transport adapters and capability testing.

5.3 Identity model

Pseudonymous identities should use cryptographic credentials rather than treating display names as authentication.

Recommended identity fields:

- Internal participant ID.
- Public pseudonymous identifier.
- Public verification key.
- Credential status.
- Revocation status.
- Optional contact information.
- Device registration references.

Private keys must not be stored in plaintext server databases.

5.4 Call Cards

Call Cards provide an alternative communication identifier that does not require publishing a conventional telephone number.

Potential capabilities:

- Public contact discovery.
- Private connection requests.
- Credential verification.
- Revocation.
- Optional service routing.
- User-controlled visibility.

A Call Card identifier is not proof of a person's legal identity.

5.5 SOS-GEO-INSPECT-01

The SOS subsystem coordinates emergency signaling and optional location evidence.

Proposed capabilities:

- User-initiated SOS activation.
- Permission-controlled geolocation.
- Timestamped location observations.
- Emergency contact routing.
- Delivery confirmation.
- Location expiration.
- Audit records.

Location must be collected only under an explicit and documented permission model, with restricted access and retention.

The VPN Map must not become an unrestricted individual surveillance system. Network diagnostics, server location, and user location are distinct data categories.

5.6 World Chat acceptance criteria

- Cross-platform message compatibility.
- Cryptographically authenticated messages.
- Message replay protection.
- Device and credential revocation.
- Offline queue recovery.
- Duplicate message handling.
- Defined delivery states.
- Permission-controlled location access.
- Documented metadata exposure.
- Independently reproducible protocol tests.

