7. EZnvoice & Payment Orchestration

Primary role: Financial transaction coordination.

EZnvoice provides a common workflow for invoices, payment requests, transaction status, and receipts.

7.1 Invoice structure

Each invoice should include:

- Unique invoice ID.
- Issuer reference.
- Recipient reference.
- Item or service description.
- Amount.
- Currency.
- Issue date.
- Expiration date.
- Payment conditions.
- Payment status.
- Supporting evidence references.

7.2 Payment state machine

CREATED
   |
PENDING_AUTHORIZATION
   |
AUTHORIZED
   |
PROCESSING
   |
CONFIRMED
   |
RECONCILED

Alternative states:

- FAILED
- EXPIRED
- CANCELLED
- REVERSED
- REFUNDED
- DISPUTED

The exact transitions depend on the payment provider and payment rail.

7.3 Payment adapter

The payment adapter should provide:

- Payment intent creation.
- Authorization.
- Execution.
- Status retrieval.
- Refund processing.
- Webhook verification.
- Reconciliation.
- Fee reporting.

Payment provider notifications must be authenticated and processed idempotently.

7.4 Financial security

- No unrestricted storage of raw payment-card credentials.
- Protected API credentials.
- Signing-key protection.
- Idempotency controls.
- Replay protection.
- Amount and currency validation.
- Transaction limits.
- Reconciliation procedures.
- Incident response.

An authorization is not equivalent to settlement. A blockchain confirmation is not equivalent to a bank settlement.

