8. Escrow Oracle Chain

Primary role: Conditional transaction execution.

Escrow coordinates the fulfillment of contractual conditions before funds or assets are released.

8.1 Escrow lifecycle

INVOICE_CREATED
       |
TERMS_ACCEPTED
       |
FUNDS_DEPOSITED
       |
CONDITIONS_PENDING
       |
   +---+---+
   |       |
VERIFIED  DISPUTED
   |       |
RELEASE   REVIEW
   |       |
SETTLED  RESOLUTION

Additional states should support cancellation, refund, expiration, and failed settlement.

8.2 Custody distinction

The system must explicitly identify whether funds are:

- Merely recorded in an internal ledger.
- Authorized by a payment provider.
- Reserved by a payment provider.
- Deposited into a smart contract.
- Held by a regulated third-party custodian.

An internal database entry is not escrow custody.

8.3 Oracle requirements

Each oracle source must define:

- Source identity.
- Evidence format.
- Verification procedure.
- Freshness requirement.
- Failure behavior.
- Conflicting evidence handling.
- Authorized reviewers.
- Emergency suspension rules.

Oracle unavailability must never automatically count as proof of fulfillment.

8.4 Smart-contract requirements

- Independent contract review.
- Access-control verification.
- Reentrancy protection where applicable.
- Replay protection.
- Defined upgrade policy.
- Emergency pause policy.
- Documented dispute handling.
- Tested recovery and refund paths.

