11. Shared Identity & Authorization

All platform services should use consistent identity and authorization principles.

11.1 Identity categories

- Anonymous visitor.
- Registered pseudonymous participant.
- Verified credential holder.
- Service account.
- Administrator.
- Independent auditor.
- Governance authority.

Verification must be scoped to the claim being established.

A verified cryptographic key does not automatically establish a verified legal identity.

11.2 Authorization model

Recommended approach:

Role-Based Access Control combined with resource-specific authorization.

Example:

Role| Permission
Participant| Own account and permitted interactions
Seller| Manage authorized listings
Buyer| Submit eligible bids
Auditor| Read approved audit evidence
Operator| Manage designated services
Administrator| Perform explicitly authorized administrative functions

Privileged actions should require additional authentication, logging, and review.

