13. Security Architecture & Threat Model

Security must be evaluated across the entire platform, not only the blockchain components.

13.1 Threat categories

Threat| Primary control
Account compromise| Strong authentication and recovery
Key theft| Protected key storage and rotation
Message interception| Authenticated encryption
Replay attacks| Nonces and idempotency
Fraudulent bids| Server-authoritative validation
Payment duplication| Idempotency and reconciliation
Oracle manipulation| Source verification and dispute handling
Contract vulnerabilities| Independent security audits
Insider abuse| Least privilege and audit trails
Data leakage| Encryption and minimization
Network outage| Store-and-forward and recovery
Service concentration| Replaceable interfaces and portability

13.2 Security release gates

No production financial execution should be enabled before:

1. Threat modeling.
2. Authentication testing.
3. Authorization testing.
4. API security testing.
5. Cryptographic implementation review.
6. Data protection assessment.
7. Incident response exercises.
8. Independent contract audit where applicable.
9. Remediation verification.
10. Release authorization.

