15. Implementation Roadmap

Development should proceed through controlled milestones.

P0 — Protocol Foundation

Objective: Establish shared technical contracts.

Deliverables:

- Master data model.
- Identity specification.
- Authorization model.
- Event envelope.
- API definitions.
- Cryptographic standards.
- Threat model.
- Repository structure.
- Development environments.

Exit criteria: Cross-system interfaces pass schema and authorization tests.

P1 — World Chat & Mesh Prototype

Objective: Demonstrate communication independently of financial execution.

Deliverables:

- Pseudonymous identity.
- Call Cards.
- Personal Channel.
- Message schemas.
- Local peer exchange.
- Store-and-forward.
- Revocation.
- Basic synchronization.

Exit criteria: Web and Android clients exchange compatible authenticated messages, including tested offline scenarios.

P2 — Integrity Ledger & Xenograph

Objective: Establish verifiable event records.

Deliverables:

- Event ingestion.
- Hash generation.
- Digital signatures.
- Event sequencing.
- Evidence references.
- Reconciliation.
- Analytical reports.

Exit criteria: Independent verification reproduces selected event-integrity results.

P3 — Card Conduit

Objective: Implement deterministic interactive mechanics.

Deliverables:

- Card registry.
- Inventory.
- Rule engine.
- Energy relay.
- Color combinations.
- Surge mechanics.
- Game-state recording.

Exit criteria: Rule-based gameplay and inventory transitions pass reproducibility and integrity tests.

P4 — EZnvoice & Payments

Objective: Demonstrate controlled payment orchestration.

Deliverables:

- Invoice service.
- Payment adapter.
- Sandbox transactions.
- Webhook verification.
- Idempotency.
- Refund handling.
- Reconciliation.

Exit criteria: Repeated requests, failures, reversals, and reconciliation scenarios pass testing.

P5 — Escrow & Auction

Objective: Introduce conditional asset exchange.

Deliverables:

- Escrow state machine.
- Smart-contract test deployment.
- Oracle interfaces.
- Dispute workflow.
- Auction listing.
- Bid validation.
- Settlement coordination.

Exit criteria: Independent security review, tested dispute paths, and successful transaction reconciliation.

P6 — Controlled Pilot

Objective: Evaluate the integrated platform.

Deliverables:

- Limited participant onboarding.
- Operational monitoring.
- Security assessment.
- User accessibility evaluation.
- Performance testing.
- Governance review.
- Pilot reporting.

Exit criteria: Documented acceptance evidence and authorization for the next deployment stage.

