17. Governance & Institutional Accountability

The platform should distinguish technical authority, financial authority, and governance authority.

17.1 Governance requirements

- Documented administrative permissions.
- Independent review of privileged actions.
- Defined dispute-resolution procedures.
- Published policy versions.
- Evidence-preservation procedures.
- Conflict-of-interest disclosure.
- Incident reporting.
- User appeals.
- Change-management records.

17.2 Institutional Communication Integrity

Communications and administrative decisions should preserve:

- Original submission.
- Submission timestamp.
- Responsible recipient.
- Acknowledgment status.
- Subsequent amendments.
- Supporting evidence.
- Decision authority.
- Final disposition.

The system should distinguish receipt, acknowledgment, review, and resolution.

17.3 Governance principle

Institutional authority does not replace documentary evidence.

A recorded decision must remain distinguishable from the evidence used to support it.

